anizations Athletics Blue Devil Bands Greek Life Student Veterans Group Student Government Blue Devil Motorsports Student Support Career Services Clinical Counseling Office of International Programs One Stop Center Student Access and Accommodations Student Accounts LGBT Resource Center ABOUT Contact Us Campus Map Directions Facilities Consumer Information Office of the President Marketing Job Openings Faculty and Staff Resources Employee Handbooks Faculty and Staff Directory Organizational Chart Staff Senate Human Resources 25Live Title IX Community Programs Facility Rental High School Summer Programs Marburger STEM Center Robofest History NEWS CALENDAR ALUMNI GIVING FACULTY + STAFF BANNERWEB EHELP Search Job Postings Home » Job Postings » Assistant Football Coach Assistant Football Coach Date Posted: July 29, 2026 Position Number: AF9993 Hiring Supervisor: Director of Athletics Job Type: Staff Employment Type: Full-Time Department: Athletics » Job Description JOB TITLE: Assistant Football Coach POSITION NUMBER : AF9993 HIRING SUPERVISOR: Director of Athletics DEPARTMENT: Athletics TYPE: Full-Time SUMMARY: Lawrence Technological University, an NAIA Institution and member of the Wolverine Hoosier Athletic Conference and the Mid-States Football Association is accepting applications for an Assistant Football Coach. Reporting to the Head Football Coach, the Assistant Football Coach supports the mission of the college by assisting all aspects of the College’s football program, developing and executing effective coaching strategies, recruiting talented student-athletes and retaining them, assisting with team practices and games, and fostering a positive team culture. Serves as a Campus Security Authority as outlined by the Clery Act. ESSENTIAL DUTIES and RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop and Coach the Quarterbacks. Run position Meetings with the QBs Recruiting areas in Michigan, Ohio, and anywhere else the head coach and recruiting coordinator sends you. Evaluate and recruit qualified student-athletes. Assist with planning, organizing, and conducting all workouts, meetings, and practices. Organize game preparation, including film breakdown and development of game plans, scouting reports, and responsible for all sideline/box clipboards and forms used. Ensure all coaching assignments are carried out during daily workouts, practices, and competitions to maximize athletic performance. In charge of summer high school football camp Assist in the coordination of annual summer camps, recruitment trips, and on-campus recruitment events Communicate and collaborate with departments across campus to ensure student-athlete Monitor academic progress of the team and individual student-athletes. Mentor student athletes through academic and athletic challenges. Participate in fundraising events. Other duties assigned by the Head Coach, Coordinators, or Athletic Department. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: Oversight of part-time, graduate assistants, and volunteer coaches. Must have exemplary ethical conduct and a commitment to follow all applicable NAIA and Mid-States Conference rules and regulations. Must follow all athletic and football staff policies and procedures. Must have the ability to work effectively in a collaborative effort to maintain the mission, vision, and objectives of the athletics department. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE: A Bachelor’s degree is required. Minimum of three years coaching experience in the collegiate setting and/or at a highly respected high school program. Experience coaching Quarterbacks. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. The ability to work non-traditional hours, including late night and weekends. Knowledge and skill to evaluate and assess student-athlete’s skills and abilities. Enthusiasm and willingness to develop, initiate, and actively recruit, retain, and develop student-athletes. Commitment to work and educate inclusively with a diverse student population. Sound administrative and supervisory skills. Lawrence Technological University (LTU) conducts pre-employment screening on initial candidates for all positions, which may include but is not limited to, a criminal background check, verification of academic credentials, license, certifications, and/or verification of work history.  Lawrence Technological University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. » How to Apply Please send cover letter and resume to Mary Ann Meltzer at mmeltzer@ltu.edu . 1 800 225 5588 21000 West Ten Mile Road Southfield, MI, 48075-1058 Instagram Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Facebook-f X-twitter Tiktok Linkedin Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Quick Links News Calendar Alumni Giving Faculty + Staff BannerWeb eHelp Library News Calendar Alumni Giving Faculty + Staff BannerWeb eHelp Library Admissions Apply Explore + Visit Academics Programs Course Catalog Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Apply Explore + Visit Academics Programs Course Catalog Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Student Life Housing Student Support Student Organizations Athletics Bookstore Library Housing Student Support Student Organizations Athletics Bookstore Library About Contact Us Campus Map Job Openings Research + Economic Development Office of the President Office of the Provost Marketing Privacy Policy Contact Us Campus Map Job Openings Research + Economic Development Office of the President Office of the Provost Marketing Privacy Policy ©2026 Lawrence Technological University. All Rights Reserved. Title IX Sitemap Title IX Sitemap"
